<title>UK: Banco General sets $100 mln five-year bond. [CORRECTED 15:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Banco General sets $100 mln five-year bond. [CORRECTED 15:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager CSFB.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANCO GENERAL SA</p>
<p> AMT    $100 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    01.AUG.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE  S-06.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.25	REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+160-170 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>(Lead manager corrects pay date from August 4 to August 6.)</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BBB-	DENOMS (K) 10-250    SALE LIMITS US/UK/PA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  PANAMA    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    50 BP     SELL CONC  75 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.0 PCT JULY 2002 BOND</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
